'''AWB-X''' is a cross-platform rewrite of [[Wikipedia:AutoWikiBrowser|AutoWikiBrowser]] (AWB), the semi-automated editor. It runs on '''Linux, macOS and Windows''' and is meant for every Wikipedia language, including right-to-left scripts (Arabic, Hebrew, Persian), Indic scripts (Malayalam, Hindi) and Chinese, Japanese and Korean.

AWB-X is '''in development and not yet released'''. This page describes how it behaves on the wiki so that editors and server operators know what to expect, and how to reach its developers.

== How it relates to AutoWikiBrowser ==
AWB-X keeps AWB's behaviour: the same general fixes, typo fixing (using [[Wikipedia:AutoWikiBrowser/Typos]]), find and replace, list making and skip options. AWB's own unit tests are run against AWB-X to check that its fixes give the same results.

What is different:
* It is written in Python with the Qt toolkit instead of .NET and Windows Forms, so it does not need Windows.
* Regular expressions use full Unicode rules: words in Malayalam, Hindi and Persian (with ZWNJ) are not split, and characters outside the Basic Multilingual Plane count as one character.
* Every rule runs with a time limit, so a slow rule is skipped and reported instead of freezing the program.
* Previews and the visual editor open in your web browser.

== Using it on a wiki ==
AWB-X follows the same [[Wikipedia:AutoWikiBrowser#Rules of use|rules of use]] as AWB. You are responsible for every edit you save with it.

=== Approval (CheckPage) ===
AWB-X uses AWB's existing approval system and does not add one of its own:
* On each wiki it reads <code>Project:AutoWikiBrowser/CheckPageJSON</code> and <code>Project:AutoWikiBrowser/Config</code>. If your account is not approved there, AWB-X will not save edits.
* It also reads the global page [[Wikipedia:AutoWikiBrowser/CheckPage/VersionJSON]], so names blocked from AWB everywhere are also blocked from AWB-X.
* Bot mode is available only to accounts listed under <code>enabledbots</code>.

=== Logging in ===
Log in with a [[Special:BotPasswords|bot password]]. AWB-X does not store passwords in its settings file. If you ask it to remember a password, it keeps it in your operating system's keychain (Keychain on macOS, Credential Manager on Windows, Secret Service/KWallet on Linux).

== For server operators ==
AWB-X uses the MediaWiki Action API through [[mw:Manual:Pywikibot|Pywikibot]]. It:
* sends a User-Agent of the form <code>AWB-X/''version'' (''link to this page''; ''wiki''; User:''account'') Pywikibot/''version'' …</code>;
* sends <code>maxlag=5</code> with edits and waits when the servers are lagged;
* sends <code>assert=user</code>, <code>baserevid</code> and the base timestamp with every save, so edit conflicts are detected and logged-out edits are refused;
* fetches Wikidata items in batches of 50.

If AWB-X misbehaves on your wiki, please leave a message on [[{{TALKPAGENAME}}|the talk page]].

